<%# Receivables aging — Finance's collection priority list (module 8 part 8.3).
    PRD §5.2: "Aging report view (30/60/90/120+ day buckets), sortable by amount — Finance's
    collection priority list." PRD §5.4 names the same report. Screen map: Reports | Aging.

    READ THIS BEFORE EDITING. Three measured defects shape this page:

    1. The tiles and the table are built from ONE result set in the route (`bucketTiles`
       rolls the same `q.receivableAging` rows up), so a bucket tile can never disagree with
       the rows beneath it.

    2. The "cannot be dated" group is NOT a bucket and is NOT at the bottom of the chase
       order. `v_aging` deliberately EXCLUDES undatable claims (migration 020) because the
       old CASE fell through to '120_plus' and reported an undated invoice as the most
       overdue item on the list. They are a data-quality to-do, so they get their own
       labelled card that says "fix the data", not a red urgency chip.

    3. Retainage is its own tile (PRD §5.2: "retainage held separately (never buried in
       regular AR)"), read from the register rather than from the aging list, so a claim
       that has been settled but is still retained keeps its figure.

    Title and sub-title come from `page()` in routes/reporting.js. %>
<% if (typeof project === 'undefined' || !project) { %>
<div class="card"><div class="fbody">
  <p class="dim">No project is in scope for your account, so there is nothing to age.</p>
</div></div>
<% } else { %>

<% const overdueRows = rows.filter(function(r){ return (r.overdue_days || 0) > 0; }); %>

<div class="grid k4">
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-book"/></svg>Outstanding</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= fmt(rows.reduce(function(a,r){ return a + (r.outstanding_amount||0); }, 0)) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= rows.length %> open claim<%= rows.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %> — money we are owed</div></div>
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg>Past its terms</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= fmt(overdueRows.reduce(function(a,r){ return a + (r.outstanding_amount||0); }, 0)) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= overdueRows.length %> claim<%= overdueRows.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %> over the due date — chase these</div></div>
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-cash"/></svg>Retainage held</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= fmt(retainage) %></div>
    <div class="f">Held back, not yet collectable — kept out of the totals above</div></div>
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-file"/></svg>Cannot be dated</div>
    <div class="v"><%= noDate.length %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= noDate.length ? 'No invoice date — these cannot be aged' : 'Every claim has a date' %></div></div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>Collection priority</h2>
    <span class="r">
      Sort:
      <% Object.keys(sortLabels).forEach(function(k, i){ %><%= i ? ' · ' : '' %><a href="/reports/aging?sort=<%= k %>" class="<%= sort === k ? 'on' : '' %>"><%= sortLabels[k] %></a><% }); %>
    </span>
  </div>
  <% if (!rows.length) { %>
  <div class="fbody"><p class="dim">Nothing is outstanding on this project. Every claim has been
    settled, so there is no collection list to work.</p></div>
  <% } else { %>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr>
      <th>Document</th><th>Invoice date</th><th>Due</th><th>Terms</th>
      <th class="r">Age</th><th class="r">Overdue</th><th class="r">Outstanding</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% rows.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="mono"><%= r.document_no %></span>
          <% if (r.has_retainage) { %><span class="chip nt">retainage held</span><% } %></td>
        <td class="mono"><%= r.invoice_date %></td>
        <td class="mono">
          <% if (r.due_date) { %><%= r.due_date %>
            <% if (r.terms_source) { %><span class="dim">(<%= r.terms_source %>, <%= r.terms_days %>d)</span><% } %>
          <% } else { %><span class="dim">—</span><% } %>
        </td>
        <td class="mono"><%= r.terms_days == null ? '—' : r.terms_days + 'd' %></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= r.days_aged == null ? '—' : Math.floor(r.days_aged) %></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= r.overdue_days == null ? '—' : r.overdue_days %></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= fmt(r.outstanding_amount) %></td>
      </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <% } %>
</div>

<div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));margin-top:12px">
  <% tiles.forEach(function(t){ %>
  <div class="card kpi">
    <div class="lbl"><%= t.label %></div>
    <div class="v mono sm"><%= fmt(t.total) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= t.n %> claim<%= t.n === 1 ? '' : 's' %><%= t.note ? ' · ' + t.note : '' %></div>
  </div>
  <% }); %>
</div>

<% if (noDate.length) { %>
<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>Cannot be dated — fix the data</h2>
    <span class="r">Not aged, and never counted as overdue</span>
  </div>
  <div class="fbody" style="padding-bottom:0">
    <p class="dim">These claims have money outstanding but no invoice date, so there is no age to
      report. They are held out of the buckets above on purpose — an undated invoice is not the
      most overdue item on the list, it is a record that needs a date. Enter the date on the entry
      screen and each one drops into its real bucket.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr>
      <th>Document</th><th class="r">Billed</th><th class="r">Paid</th>
      <th class="r">Retainage</th><th class="r">Outstanding</th><th>Terms</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% noDate.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="mono"><%= r.document_no %></span></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= fmt(r.billed_amount) %></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= fmt(r.paid_amount) %></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= fmt(r.retainage_amount) %></td>
        <td class="r mono"><%= fmt(r.outstanding_amount) %></td>
        <td class="mono"><%= r.terms_days == null ? '—' : r.terms_days + 'd (' + r.terms_source + ')' %></td>
      </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div>
<% } %>

<% } %>
